Feature: Starting and stopping a game
  G starts a [[pylon race]] and T starts a game of [[tag]]. Each game starts in the same way.
  All the planes go back to the hands of their pilots, with a fresh battery, and the game
  waits while you get ready: set up, arm and throw your plane. When you take off, the game
  panel counts down from 5. At GO the computer pilots throw their planes, one each second, and
  the game clock runs from GO. Press the key of the game
  again to stop it. To start a game again from the beginning, press its key two times.

  Expectation: G starts a race
    Given the game is not a race
    When the pilot starts a race
    Then the game is a race
    And the game clock is waiting for takeoff
    And the plane is in hand
    And the opponents are in hand
    And the lap count is 0
    And the cut count is 0

  Expectation: T starts a game of tag
    You are [[it]] first, so you start the game as the chaser.
    Given the game is not tag
    When the pilot starts a game of tag
    Then the game is tag
    And the game clock is waiting for takeoff
    And the plane is in hand
    And the opponents are in hand
    And the chaser is you

  Expectation: The key of the game stops it
    The planes of the computer pilots go away, and you fly freely.
    Given the game is not free flight
    When the pilot ends the game
    Then the game is free flight
    And the game clock is off

  Expectation: The game waits for you to take off
    The preflight is yours to do: the countdown does not start until your plane is in the air.
    Given the game clock is waiting for takeoff
    And the plane is in hand
    When the pilot throws the plane with the throttle
    Then the game clock is counting down

  Expectation: At GO the computer pilots throw their planes
    Given the game clock is counting down
    When the countdown ends
    Then the game clock is running
    And the opponents are flying
